{"title":"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, construct the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679d0a6d6cef45b71d1a66078ca115bdca133558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"11\" /> by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/494d6655f35986e8d2726a5d96cb77f7d04497a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=x_n \\left(x_n + \\frac{1}{n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578cf6c5b8058f6f8e6369416da6dcaf73f8fc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />.  Prove that there exists exactly one value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a846048a57af68ba5eb51fca376c9fc477f48328.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_&lt;x_n&lt;x_{n+1}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By recursive substitution, one can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b80cfc1d4ff1206a8cf031e3acd1f9b9f187b4b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=P_n(x_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> , where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is a polynomial with non-negative coefficients and zero constant term. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43d7261abb6ce26070a4e5d08704cd32a39fede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is strictly increasing in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/6695592fec5d1f2682eae1ca40d1ccc81e431079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,+\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> , and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc5bea6326777567ea2e98a6c95e0f4772616b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x_1 \\rightarrow + \\infty} P_n(x_1)=+\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"162\" height=\"26\" />. We can therefore define the inverse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c2e4c156a5db18d835e0f05d7fb75fe618e027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c51a4acedda645113145d008dbfb50d35f1da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/6695592fec5d1f2682eae1ca40d1ccc81e431079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,+\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f3f41b7332a9ab80acc781f8643eff1082ccc45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=P_n^{-1}(x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbdd4a7e2e0f88473062ce1a4f3ba2f52d0863a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n^{-1}(0)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c2e4c156a5db18d835e0f05d7fb75fe618e027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> is strictly increasing in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/9/6695592fec5d1f2682eae1ca40d1ccc81e431079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,+\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da52e13bb5c46125ebff4fe295422d1b7190a8db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\lim_{x_1 \\rightarrow + \\infty} P_n^{-1}(x_1) =+\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"173\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>Denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/8/318cc15d0ca8e818cb522b0d0e19cb9f3daba073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle a_n=P_n^{-1}(1-\\frac{1}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb236c97f779a6197f36c23d679680e5b3b89f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n=P_n^{-1}(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" />. By the monotonicity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c2e4c156a5db18d835e0f05d7fb75fe618e027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_n^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"19\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fdebf77b164e07a995960269b97007ed6f49921.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&lt;b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Note that:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d11cdb84fe7ad7fa40c5cc5c02c7f0f5e60ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x_n&lt;x_{n+1} \\Leftrightarrow x_n&gt;1-\\frac{1}{n} \\Leftrightarrow P_n^{-1}(x_n)&gt;P_n^{-1}(1-\\frac{1}{n}) \\Leftrightarrow x_1&gt;a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"499\" height=\"38\" />;\n(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/5/0353c7812159805acc4861bc89974aa38bbb82c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x_n&lt;1 \\Leftrightarrow P_n^{-1}(x_n)&lt;P_n^{-1}(1) \\Leftrightarrow x_1&lt;b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"312\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11beecac27d42bf99b42acaa0606c48d0325eb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_n&lt;x_{n+1}&lt;1,\\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"17\" /> holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df21ea8b0dc1c6893b339936a7bd3cb2fc67ea6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&lt;x_1&lt;b_n,\\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae0b18f3da9ff9930bff38f7afe0d60c32f24c75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle x_1 \\in \\bigcap_{n=1}^{+\\infty}(a_n,b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"125\" height=\"55\" />. We need to show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7037ac41c34cc3e7bd06e41f579785d09e24f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{n=1}^{+\\infty}(a_n,b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"81\" height=\"50\" /> is a singleton. We have:\n</p><p>(c) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c36f46bb8ed8ad52fe7686ff8a634c1a03c73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a51ef2adaa1f9e613fbff12cce5fda713a36529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=1-\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81cc2780066be5eb07c3535e3e1f6fc2e104f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1-\\frac{1}{n}&lt;1-\\frac{1}{n+1}=P_{n+1}(a_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"318\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e996810d7f6ea11196ffa0b89d75841e555e6714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&lt;a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/0/6b077b4cc119c24404920248e0d446e4208b77a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&lt;a_{n+1},\\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />; and\n(d) if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944612cff044387e25e8e235ca8910f723561acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/5375291443412da51f87fce294375d38582fd5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151f129e08a565cb84efaf423a123e5546d5212f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1+\\frac{1}{n}&gt;1=P_{n+1}(b_{n+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"248\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c852cfa5ec2bfe72d809bae787d83f818a55556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&gt;b_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9f8a5caae5c0d09037d77e65c9b8c098c4891c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n&gt;b_{n+1},\\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />; and\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54ce8009902020c7be413c15b70cec9620e93de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n&lt;a_{n+1}&lt;b_{n+1}&lt;b_n, \\forall n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, the two sequences <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d812313e0d16f63360616f841da92276ec2eaa6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n=1}^{+\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae3710ac365636a8ca6da5ead91c231a6aa8537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{b_n\\}_{n=1}^{+\\infty}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"19\" /> converge, and their limits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66b776ccefeb6ed39992028c1418f795e54602cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/3/853240ee1bae3698b91735be674b9f7e5c3ef9a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\bigcap_{n=1}^{+\\infty}(a_n,b_n)=[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"140\" height=\"50\" /> is non-empty, which demonstrates the existence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Now, suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/48230e6256393316a62ac5c9434d23114ee92826.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leq x_1 \\leq x_1&#39; \\leq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ab2e6786c130c165fecaa962d8bf7a1a24039e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}&#39;-x_{n+1} = (x_n&#39;-x_n)(x_n&#39;+x_n+\\frac{1}{n}) \\geq (x_n&#39;-x_n)(2-\\frac{1}{n}) \\geq (x_n&#39;-x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"564\" height=\"37\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a5fac18595dc1c145f676cd8638cc59a6715761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n&#39;-x_n \\geq x_1&#39;-x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97f0ff2050998fbe2ab6763fb6c71e5b1e2ea07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{n}&lt;x_n \\leq x_n&#39;&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/8460af77f980a433745e84e9fabcc8d600b33600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq x_n&#39;-x_n&lt;\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"135\" height=\"38\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd95e343c62b52042a0d57907d755a75ba24f799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\displaystyle \\lim_{n \\rightarrow +\\infty}(x_n&#39;-x_n)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"153\" height=\"26\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/8/3d85b376375a5bcf9ce1985c925217f26a5e4024.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&#39; \\leq x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, proving unicity.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by DAFR. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p2751173\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the interval of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd79133b459d4ad751d6cf5d06ebdf1939e12883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\textless x \\textless 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9338ea2b6dc57275f4d1ca750b74901d7bb0377a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />, we will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efebfeedb28b8203080618bfe13a8a56d37f1e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n \\textless x_{n+1} \\textless 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. (That is, the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> which make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> \"work\"). We must prove these intervals intersect at one point.\n</p><p>First, I prove they intersect. Notice that as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> increases, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> do too. So if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/d/4fd822cd3ebe55e5394694cd72de63b033cf2430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n=(a_n,b_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> it is easy to see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2b00cfbe98d3c738a914581e6b2fda87262d52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"10\" /> will give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320014e02bc4482bdaa75231cd28021e3764ff56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=x_{n+1}=1-1/n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57fb0346cb24e6f331f10adeaddbd5c772821aa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_n=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> will give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b35793607e797e8e3fb887c9fd8129d46f5e0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> (the \"extremal\" values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> can take are given by the extremal values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> can take).\n</p><p>But if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2b00cfbe98d3c738a914581e6b2fda87262d52c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"10\" /> we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e9a2bc3c7c064b0a62ea36d98ad2bc2e5c5df2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} \\textless 1-1/(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9eacbec9d1ea02d5808873ea601a3b1534bea2e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} \\textgreater x_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944612cff044387e25e8e235ca8910f723561acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b35793607e797e8e3fb887c9fd8129d46f5e0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> which gives a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1b5c3dd3fb70379ba309ec109ff2e59f0c6db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> too big. So basically when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> only barely works for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bdee5e53970edceae79323e26921a8d62d3f76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />, it won't work for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1b5c3dd3fb70379ba309ec109ff2e59f0c6db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/1/ab196eb1d2c6df8f8bb47caddcafc44d8fac9097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df770e3d462055fa01655d3c2720d295eed74e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>So we have an infinite sequence of open intervals, each contained inside the previous one. Therefore their intersection must contain at least one number. This guarantees the existence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>But, we must prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> can't take two different values. Suppose it could. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967e68bee082c5056a1770e7ad94f40ed1645101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" /> both work. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the sequence generated by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11fe623c8d58828616bd985a407411f56ac298fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> the sequence generated by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9195deb3f3086a38e69264c264929d36fc8e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_i=x_i&#39;-x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> (wlog <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1348afef1cbededf7fd83f88450236260a8bf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\textless b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />). Then we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49ddf3f41de6caf33fc06d01e46def82dde97d25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l_{n+1}=l_n(2x_n+l_n+1/n) \\textgreater l_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb50192a672c8bed7b4968ad9782eae37e3284d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x_n \\textgreater 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9f061a43967092d04ff479980ce99751fac3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n \\textgreater 1-1/n \\ge 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. So there exists a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74a9234863a31ef2fb81c8b302de1361771a6081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k&#39; \\ge x_k+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. But since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c37fe80563fe15531186e9e87837d032aa6bd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_k, x_k&#39; \\in (1-1/k, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, this is impossible. So we're done.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by JuanOrtiz. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p3492644\">[2]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider, now, the following observations:\n</p><p>(a) If, at any point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15f969ce0015fd9cec208303f514b14da5803299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}\\le x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />, then from here we know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07cc540b3806ee5a297788b52044bbda787bdb43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n\\le 1-\\frac{1}{n},\\quad x_{n+1}\\le 1-\\frac{1}{n} &lt; 1-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\to x_{n+2}&lt;x_{n+1}, \\cdots  x_m\\le 1-\\frac{1}{n} &lt; 1-\\frac{1}{m}\\to x_{m+1}&lt;x_m, \\forall m&gt;n\\]\" width=\"792\" height=\"38\" />and therefore the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> will be monotonically decreasing after one point.\n</p><p>(b) If some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> does satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c68a3563df8eb4eb94b432da33bdddbdaf88a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x_n&lt;x_{n+1}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/6284e98c142143bfc6f31a874eacac6d6c78f5ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{n}&lt;x_n&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"37\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and therefore by Squeeze's theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eae5323d98dc2f6544eab6c8842c9fe2b295107d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}x_n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"89\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>(c) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b8c300f167c3fec0d0b9003cbaf05d97a713f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/5220b2c99588bde73d16ae7655f2dac549138200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}=x_n(x_n+\\frac 1n)&gt;x_n^2\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"226\" height=\"37\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25637d819f73105857768ccda31e0bef6d85eb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+m}&gt;(x_{m+1})^{2^{m-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"23\" /> which then gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780d4879f6cba9917e9a523b2a6930c3276926f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}x_n=+\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"113\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>(d) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13fc6e422abab267c4044323541d00c88f1ce8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, then for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f56054dc8eb39730fa5d01cc2a4cffe16a2f18c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5cdf4e4d4e9d19d2624181d6d532918c7800f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1\\to\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" /> then for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (fixed), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/4725d80218b0fd05a33d9c5d480735045432b30f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n\\to\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, we can denote a mapping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/9/77968b55e13c69e9f64fbd241ebc55a5e417c0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n:\\mathbb{R}^{\\ge 0}\\to \\mathbb{R}^{\\ge 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" /> that maps <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, which is continuous and monotonically increasing, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b5e140515d12614971af7ec4cd35b9e1477963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{x\\to +\\infty} f_n(x)=+\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"145\" height=\"25\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc19ca9685e2dcc4316b6dda7d448dad7254d724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is bijective.\n</p><p>Let's first show uniqueness. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c2c794324d43d075a8cf011879e5360ca9731eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{y_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> are both such sequences. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bf1f274cb032515f2861dc5574cd35752ebc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}x_n=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}y_n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"169\" height=\"23\" /> and suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fbd8c1cb4472bd14376c0f980ff5feaf890e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1&gt;x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. Then for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f870eab7127bca40f1ddff08ab2982a34d847a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}} = \\frac{y_n(y_n+\\frac 1n)}{x_n(x_n+\\frac 1n)}&gt;\\frac{y_n}{x_n}\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"47\" /> so inductively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13b913656782e058e1f2895a2eb06f8fb0e7396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}}&gt;(\\frac{y_{1}}{x_{1}})^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714c91f2c7dcef1ddc6a0d558e4753538af83381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{y_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}}=+\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" />.\nHowever, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bf1f274cb032515f2861dc5574cd35752ebc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}x_n=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}y_n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"169\" height=\"23\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d4440dd6e2923f7b62ce7fce99708b67ba851a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{y_{n+1}}{x_{n+1}}=\\frac{1}{1}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"147\" height=\"41\" />, contradiction.\nHence, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies this must be unique.\n</p><p>Next, let's show existence. We have seen from above that, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fbd8c1cb4472bd14376c0f980ff5feaf890e64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1&gt;x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e072dffe72d4df122713aced34ea2bc30af9f99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_n&gt;x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/7/cb7746ce3c07f85d69a1ea172a21d91cab788104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5dd8e5b43242c6153db18b4123a70c811990b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is monotonically increasing after some point. Suppose no such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> exists. Let\n\\[\nA=\\{x_1: \\exists n: x_{n+1}&lt;x_n\\}\\qquad B=\\{x_1: \\exists n: x_n&gt;1\\}\n\\]then if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/6550276377d461aa90435ac0d2f08dfbef079a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44bdc91f7bb4006c13b319b9a3682b4b89da1b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d187bbf8ff2d63ac9490e9026fb65b0f45f47860.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> and similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9c821e4a74612f57bd6bbd6390ceded859944f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf0221ead82892800d789a75c60cb29d3062488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef78b11efa91835a358388bd7c7b1c54da1bb4b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" />. Notice also an wasy fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/5135341f2d00f3a8675fc1be7f82b016d65db769.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is bounded. Define, now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/7186bfc63ec37e2f5cc3f8aa12bb14c03dc295b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=glb(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. As we assumed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980677c5c1d1efda4f4270dbe2f7068a06aaea72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\cup B=\\mathbb{R}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" />, this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/749da0551aff98b581526af9a5fedf67041a9c50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&lt;c\\to x_1\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999c1297b238aa88b6a9d0d7cc485e52eba2fe3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1&gt;c\\to x_1\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" />. It remains to ask whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645ce1d6ed9b85b13d81016a6f37c0c4297a5594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5e324c521e04ca0bb22ecf00fbbae5d7890fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645ce1d6ed9b85b13d81016a6f37c0c4297a5594.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, then for this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7fcc6f0458fb1e69a87b33cd2c5df1501b4c17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1:=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/7/507cd836d7996da0195be48f1f77cbb75c166de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n\\le 1-\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8cc7d072686348f07002d9bdd717d78318284e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}&lt;1-\\frac{1}{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"136\" height=\"38\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f63d1033d199d9227bee861039158e0f80089285.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> be such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a627b47359d5a7e8f1764280e149b5ab4d782735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1}&lt;y_{n+1}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />. By above, there's exactly one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517bdcef79e2f193071018fb867d729167cffbf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n+1}(y_1)&lt;y_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, and notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b86f02959dbe4cfd1da13c501caed193baaffbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1&gt;x_1=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" /> by the monotonicity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e6896e1acda7d83cfc277778843cb210c63a49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" />. This means that there exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988bbb813f1bc55122ad803c678807be32e9c55c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1&gt;c\\in A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, contradicting the definition of glb. A similar contradiction (but opposite direction) can also be established for the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/5/9c5e324c521e04ca0bb22ecf00fbbae5d7890fe9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\in B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is neither in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33af316d831584176cec4aa611abf0e8c2781b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" /> should satisfy the problem condition. Q.E.D.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by Anzoteh. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p18824436\">[3]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017175245\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.056 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.070 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 769/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 33131/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.631      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.631      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11269:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017175245 and revision id 229951. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}